    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You qualify sales leads for this service:\n\"AI automation for small businesses: chatbots that answer customer enquiries on WhatsApp, Telegram or a website, plus automated enquiry handling and booking.\"\n\nBusiness:\n- Name: {{ $json.title }}\n- Category: {{ $json.categoryName }}\n- Address: {{ $json.address }}\n- Phone: {{ $json.phone || 'none listed' }}\n- Website: {{ $json.website || 'none listed' }}\n- Google rating: {{ $json.totalScore || 'none' }} from {{ $json.reviewsCount || 0 }} reviews\n\nScore this lead from 1 (poor fit) to 10 (excellent fit) using these signals:\n- Reachable: a phone number is listed (essential; without one, score 3 or lower)\n- Busy: many reviews means many customer enquiries, so more value from automation\n- Room to improve: no website or a basic online presence means a stronger need for digital help\n- Customer-facing: businesses that take bookings or answer lots of questions benefit most\n- Data quality: if the name and category don't match, or the listing looks like spam/keyword-stuffed, score 4 or lower and say so in the reason.\n- Fewer than 5 reviews: maximum score 6.\nCalculate the score with these points (start at 5):\n+2 if 50 or more reviews; +1 if 10–49 reviews; −1 if fewer than 5 reviews\n+1 if no website, or only a WhatsApp link / free site (e.g. Google Sites, GitHub Pages)\n+1 if the business clearly takes bookings or site visits (e.g. installers, clinics, salons)\n−3 if no phone number\n−3 if the name and category don't match or the listing looks spammy\nKeep the final score between 1 and 10, and show the calculation briefly in the reason.\n\nThen write a personalised opening line for a first message FROM a freelance automation specialist TO this business:\n- Address the business by name (e.g. \"Hi BRIWECO team,\"). Never write \"Hello from <business>\".\n- Structure: greeting → ONE real detail from the data → one short sentence on the benefit → a soft question.\n-Use ONE detail only; don't combine the address with the reviews\n- Benefit to mention: replying to customer enquiries instantly, even after hours, so they don't lose jobs to competitors.\n- Under 40 words, warm and professional, at most one exclamation mark.\n- Vary the wording; do not start with \"Congratulations\".\n- Never invent facts, compliments or claims not supported by the data.\n\nExample of the right style (do not copy it word for word):\n\"Hi BRIWECO team, 15 reviews averaging 4.9 means customers trust you, and probably message you a lot. Would instant WhatsApp replies, even after hours, help you catch more of those enquiries?\"\n- \"Hi BRIWECO team, 15 reviews averaging 4.9 says customers trust you. How do you currently keep up with WhatsApp enquiries when you're out on installations?\"\n- \"Hello Novel Solar, with 93 reviews you must get a lot of questions about pricing. Would it help if those got an instant, accurate reply, even at night?\"\n- \"Hi LIMED TECH team, I help solar companies in Ibadan reply to customer enquiries instantly so fewer jobs slip away. Is that something you'd find useful?\"\nUse a different question each time.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": []
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
